Z||000003||olympic||07-29-2000||04:50 PM||||   I'm about 99% sure that the GM will try and replace the Firebird with a riced out Sunfire.   They'll add non functional ram air, a big wing, and some WS6 and other stickers and sell a million of them.   The majority of youth don't seem to be interested in all out performance anymore.  They seem to be more interested in just having a certain look, like the "riceboy" subculture.  Just look how badly Mustangs outsell F-body's.  And the F-bodys are way faster for about the same money. <P>    I think one of the big reasons that the Camaro/Trans-am sales have slipped so much is because the age group(16-25) who want these cars simply can not afford them anymore.  <P>------------------<BR>Your best...???  Losers whine about doing their best.   Winners go home and f*** the prom queen! - Sean Connery in "The Rock"||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||07-29-2000||06:53 PM||||Saw a program on TLC (the learning channel), last night. <BR>The name was The Unlikely History Of The Automobile (or something like that).<BR>Ran for about an hour. Kinda cool, but unspectacular. <BR>UNTIL... The last five minutes of the show were about the growing use of computers in the design of automobiles. There were some computer renderings of what looked like the Elise/Speedster. When the view panned around to a rear image, you could clearly see the word "FORMULA", spelled out in small block letters across the rear panel, between the tail lights.<BR>Of course, this probably doesn't mean a thing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO 3800)<P>"Some mornings, it just isn't worth<BR>chewing through the restraints."||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fformula88||07-30-2000||01:41 PM||||GM has consistently said it will not bring the Speedster to the US for.  In fact, whenever they are questioned about it, they go out of their way to try and convince that it won't.  It seems to me that they are so sensitive about it, that they must be considering it if not planning on bringing it over.  Their reaction to the idea is so strong they must be up top something.  I'd like to see it.<P>As for the Firebirds... they are just too big and expensive now.  I test drove a '98 Camaro a couple years ago and was left very unimpressed.  It was a V6, and had a lot of stuff on it.  It was a quick car... those 3800's are nice.  I cannot even imagine it in a Fiero!  But the car just wasn't that much fun to drive.  It was like driving a big ship.  It wasn't tossable at all like a Fiero.  Plus its sticker was over $23,000.  A lot of money for such a big car with hardly any interior or trunk space.  It was nice, but not nice enough to buy.  That is why the Mustang is killing it in sales.||||reg||1
